**Required blocked explanation — make the cause understandable.** Whenever you report that a bead
is blocked or deferred, lead with this plain-language contrast (adapt the wording, but preserve all
of its information):

> We are trying to **<goal or outcome>**, **but** cannot continue until:
> - **A — <concrete prerequisite>**: <owner/current status/evidence, and why it prevents the next step>
> - **B — <concrete prerequisite>**: <owner/current status/evidence, and why it prevents the next step>
> - **C — <concrete prerequisite>**: <owner/current status/evidence, and why it prevents the next step>

Use only as many prerequisites as actually exist. Then state what has already been tried and what
becomes possible once they are satisfied. Never report only “blocked”, a status/label, or
`blocked-by <id>`: translate every referenced bead, decision, permission, error, or external event
into its title/meaning and causal relationship to the intended goal. If the cause is not known, say
exactly which fact is unknown and what evidence is needed to determine it; do not invent a cause.
